# AI-Assisted Development

A major part of this project was experimenting with **AI-assisted software development**.

Instead of treating AI as a replacement for development work, it was used as a practical development assistant throughout different stages of the project.

### AI was used to support:

* Understanding front-end implementation approaches
* Generating initial code ideas
* Suggesting HTML/CSS/JavaScript implementations
* Improving page structure
* Debugging implementation problems
* Explaining unfamiliar code
* Refactoring repetitive code
* Improving responsive behavior
* Reviewing potential UI issues
* Suggesting improvements to existing implementations
* Iterating on the design and implementation

The generated suggestions were reviewed, tested, modified, and integrated into the project as appropriate.

### Development Workflow

The general workflow was:

```text
Requirement
    ↓
AI-assisted exploration
    ↓
Initial implementation
    ↓
Review and understanding
    ↓
Testing
    ↓
Debugging / modification
    ↓
Final implementation
```

This workflow helped demonstrate how modern AI tools can be integrated into normal software development tasks while keeping human review and decision-making involved.

